Message-ID: <Pine.OSX.4.64.0807300930580.4310@pol-w87351t4x8a.Princeton.EDU>

Hi Ben,

   If you are using subclass, you can use logit instead of linear.logit. 
The former is a monotone transformation of the latter, and so the 
subclasses based on quantiles would be the same whether or not you use 
logit or linear.logit. Thanks for pointing out this, though. We will have 
a further look at the code when we get a chance.

Thanks,
Kosuke

